<article class="env-definition" id="0787">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0787">Definition <span data-tag="0787">103.14.1</span>.</a> Let $\mathcal{X}$ be an algebraic stack. </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
The <em>lisse-étale site</em> of $\mathcal{X}$ is the full subcategory $\mathcal{X}_{lisse,{\acute{e}tale}}$<a class="footnotemark" href="#a0001748686" id="a0001748686-mark"><sup>1</sup></a> of $\mathcal{X}$ whose objects are those $x \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathcal{X})$ lying over a scheme $U$ such that $x : U \to \mathcal{X}$ is smooth. A covering of $\mathcal{X}_{lisse,{\acute{e}tale}}$ is a family of morphisms $\{ x_ i \to x\} _{i \in I}$ of $\mathcal{X}_{lisse,{\acute{e}tale}}$ which forms a covering of $\mathcal{X}_{\acute{e}tale}$. 
</p>
</li><li><p>
The <em>flat-fppf site</em> of $\mathcal{X}$ is the full subcategory $\mathcal{X}_{flat,fppf}$ of $\mathcal{X}$ whose objects are those $x \in \mathop{\mathrm{Ob}}\nolimits (\mathcal{X})$ lying over a scheme $U$ such that $x : U \to \mathcal{X}$ is flat. A covering of $\mathcal{X}_{flat,fppf}$ is a family of morphisms $\{ x_ i \to x\} _{i \in I}$ of $\mathcal{X}_{flat,fppf}$ which forms a covering of $\mathcal{X}_{fppf}$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
</article>